":"மடங்கி","parts":[{"text":"மடங்கி","lemma":"மடங்கி","gloss":"having retreated"}],"gloss":"having retreated","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"மாறுஎதிர்","parts":[{"text":"மாறு","lemma":"māṟu","gloss":"opposition"},{"text":"எதிர்","lemma":"etir","gloss":"against"}],"gloss":"opposing in return"},{"surface":"கழிய","parts":[{"text":"கழி","lemma":"kaḻi","gloss":"to perish"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"a","gloss":"infinitive suffix"}],"gloss":"to perish"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அலகை","parts":[{"text":"அலகை","lemma":"alakai","gloss":"shield"}],"gloss":"shield"},{"surface":"போகி","parts":[{"text":"போகு","lemma":"pōku","gloss":"to be lost"},{"text":"இ","lemma":"i","gloss":"verbal participle suffix"}],"gloss":"having gone"},{"surface":"சிதைந்து","parts":[{"text":"சிதைந்து","lemma":"சிதைந்து","gloss":"having shattered"}],"gloss":"having shattered","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"வேறு","parts":[{"text":"வேறு","lemma":"vēṟu","gloss":"different"}],"gloss":"different"},{"surface":"ஆகிய","parts":[{"text":"ஆகு","lemma":"āku","gloss":"to become"},{"text":"இய","lemma":"iya","gloss":"past participle suffix"}],"gloss":"which became"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பலகை","parts":[{"text":"பலகை","lemma":"palakai","gloss":"wooden shield"}],"gloss":"wooden shield"},{"surface":"அல்லது","parts":[{"text":"அல்லது","lemma":"allatu","gloss":"except"}],"gloss":"other than"},{"surface":"களத்து","parts":[{"text":"களத்து","lemma":"களத்து","gloss":"on the battlefield"}],"gloss":"on the battlefield","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"ஒழியதே","parts":[{"text":"ஒழி","lemma":"oḻi","gloss":"to remain"},{"text":"அது","lemma":"atu","gloss":"it"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"indeed nothing else remains"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"சேண்விளங்கு","parts":[{"text":"சேண்","lemma":"cēṇ","gloss":"distance"},{"text":"விளங்கு","lemma":"viḷaṅku","gloss":"shining"}],"gloss":"far-shining"},{"surface":"நல்லிசை","parts":[{"text":"நல்லிசை","lemma":"நல்லிசை","gloss":"good fame"}],"gloss":"good fame","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நிறீஇ","parts":[{"text":"நிறீஇ","lemma":"niṟīi","gloss":"having established"}],"gloss":"having established"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நாநவில்","parts":[{"text":"நா","lemma":"nā","gloss":"tongue"},{"text":"நவில்","lemma":"navil","gloss":"practising"}],"gloss":"tongue-practising"},{"surface":"புலவர்","parts":[{"text":"புலவர்","lemma":"pulavar","gloss":"poets"}],"gloss":"of poets"},{"surface":"வாய்","parts":[{"text":"வாய்","lemma":"vāy","gloss":"mouth"}],"gloss":"in the mouth"},{"surface":"உளானே","parts":[{"text":"உளானே","lemma":"உளானே","gloss":"he indeed is"}],"gloss":"he indeed is","split_unverified":true}]}],"literal":"and the genre and the sub-theme are not known. / When the spear passed through his chest, on this great earth / the great doer of deeds who performed his difficult duty, / if you ask, 'Where is he?' / ... / Withstanding the coming army, on his chest with a prominent garland, / as warriors struck to perform their difficult duty, / his body not even appearing, his life was lost. / As those who fought retreated and perished in opposition, / his wicker shield gone, shattered and changed, / other than his wooden shield, nothing remains on the battlefield. / Having established his far-shining good fame, / he is indeed in the mouths of poets whose tongues practice songs.","translation":"The genre and sub-theme of this poem are lost. When a spear pierced his chest, he performed his ultimate duty on this wide earth. If you ask, 'Where is that great hero now?' ... Withstanding the oncoming army, his chest adorned with a bright garland was struck by enemy warriors performing their own fierce duty. His body was shattered beyond recognition, and his life was lost. As the opposing fighters retreated and fell, his wicker shield was destroyed and broken to pieces. Now, nothing remains on the battlefield except his shattered wooden shield. But having established a far-shining, glorious fame, he lives on in the mouths of poets whose tongues praise his valor.","modern":"திணையும் துறையும் அறியப்படவில்லை. மார்பில் வேல் பாய்ந்து இறந்துபோக, இப்பெரிய பூமியில் தன் அரிய கடமையைச் செய்து முடித்த அந்தப் பெருஞ்செயலாளன் எங்கே இருக்கிறான் என்று நீ கேட்பாயானால்: ... எதிர்த்து வந்த படையைத் தடுத்து நிறுத்தி, விளங்கும் மாலையணிந்த தன் மார்பில், பகை வீரர்கள் தங்கள் அரிய கடமையைச் செய்யுமாறு தாக்கியபோது, அவனது உடம்பும் தெரியாதவாறு அவனது உயிர் அழிந்தது. அவனோடு போரிட்டவர்கள் பின்வாங்கி மடியுமாறு, அவனது தோல் கேடயம் அழிந்து சிதைந்துபோக, அவனது மரக் கேடயத்தைத் தவிர வேறு எதுவும் அந்தப் போர்க்களத்தில் எஞ்சியிருக்கவில்லை. விண்ணளவும் விளங்கும் நல்ல புகழை நிலைநிறுத்திவிட்டு, அவன் நாவால் பாடும் புலவர்களின் வாயில் வாழ்கிறான்.","explanation":"This poem belongs to the Puranaanooru collection, and its tiṇai (genre) and tuṟai (theme) are lost in the manuscripts. A speaker, likely a bard or a fellow warrior, is answering someone who asks about the whereabouts of a great hero who died in battle. The speaker explains that the hero stood firm against the oncoming enemy, receiving spear thrusts directly to his chest. His body was so utterly destroyed in the fierce combat that nothing of him remains on the battlefield except his shattered wooden shield. However, the hero is not truly gone; by sacrificing his life for his duty, he established an enduring fame and now lives forever in the songs of the poets.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}